    <bpmn:process id="W_W687" name="W687. Document Template Management &amp; Version Control" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New document type needed; existing template requires update (regulatory change, branding update, process improvement)
Frequency: Template creation: ad-hoc (~5–10 new templates/year); template updates: quarterly review cycle; version control: continuous
Volume: ~150–200 active document templates across all departments; ~20–30 template updates/year
Owner: ERP Administrator (technical); Department Heads (content)
Participants: Legal, Compliance, Department SMEs, Brand/Marketing
Source: workflow W687 — Document Template Management &amp; Version Control</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W687_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W687_Lane1" name="Department SME">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W687_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W687_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W687_Lane2" name="ERP Administrator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W687_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W687_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W687_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W687_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W687_Lane3" name="Legal">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W687_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W687_Lane4" name="Department Head">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W687_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W687_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W687_Start6" name="New document type needed; existing template requires update (regulatory change, branding…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W687_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W687_Task7" name="Template request">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Template request: Department Head or SME submits template creation or update request via service portal: specifies document type, purpose, target users, required fields, regulatory requirements (BIR format, DOLE requirements, DENR forms)
Responsible (R): Department SME
Accountable (A): Department Head
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W687_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W687_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W687_Task8" name="Template design">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Template design: ERP Administrator or designated template designer creates template in ERP document engine: defines fields (static text, dynamic merge fields from ERP data, calculated fields), layout, formatting, header/footer (BuildRight branding, entity-specific details), and output format (PDF, Excel, print)
Responsible (R): ERP Administrator
Accountable (A): Department Head
Duration: 2-4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W687_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W687_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W687_Task9" name="Legal &amp; compliance review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Legal &amp; compliance review: for templates with regulatory or legal implications (contracts, BIR forms, employment documents, safety forms): Legal reviews language and mandatory disclosures; Compliance verifies alignment with BIR, DOLE, DENR, SEC requirements; Brand/Marketing verifies corporate identity standards
Responsible (R): Legal / Compliance
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 1-3 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W687_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W687_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W687_Task10" name="Testing &amp; validation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Testing &amp; validation: test template with sample data in UAT environment: verify dynamic field population (customer name, amounts, dates), formatting, page breaks, BIR-mandated print positions; validate output across print, PDF, and email channels
Responsible (R): ERP Administrator
Accountable (A): Department SME
Duration: 2-4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W687_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W687_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W687_Task11" name="Version control &amp; publishing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Version control &amp; publishing: ERP Administrator assigns version number (e.g., v2.1), records change log (what changed, why, who approved), publishes to production template library, and archives previous version with &quot;superseded&quot; status; system prevents use of superseded templates
Responsible (R): ERP Administrator
Accountable (A): Department Head
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W687_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W687_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W687_Task12" name="Distribution &amp; training">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Distribution &amp; training: published template is available to all authorized users enterprise-wide; for significant changes, Department Head communicates changes to affected users; for BIR or regulatory template changes, Compliance issues mandatory compliance bulletin to all locations
Responsible (R): Department Head / Compliance
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 1-2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W687_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W687_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W687_Task13" name="Quarterly template audit">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Quarterly template audit: ERP Administrator runs template usage report: identifies templates not used in &gt;6 months (candidates for deactivation), templates being bypassed (users creating documents outside template system), and templates approaching regulatory review dates (e.g., annual BIR form updates); presents findings to Department Heads
Responsible (R): ERP Administrator
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 4 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W687_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W687_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W687_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W687_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W687_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-333 (ensure controlled execution — Document &amp; Knowledge Management (PA-30.3).) | - operational: (Word/Excel) to avoid perceived template rigidity, creating compliance and brand consistency risks
Owner: ERP Administrator (technical); Department Heads (content)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W687_Assoc16" sourceRef="W687_Annotation15" targetRef="W687_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W687_Flow17" sourceRef="W687_Start6" targetRef="W687_Task7" />
