    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W688" name="W688. Contract &amp; Agreement Lifecycle Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New contract or agreement required; existing contract approaching renewal/expiry; amendment or termination request
Frequency: ~30–50 new contracts/month; ~100–150 active contract renewals/year; ~20–30 amendments/year
Volume: ~1,100–1,400 active contracts across all entities (~800 vendor supply agreements, ~205 store leases, plus 3PL/IT, service, customer, partnership MOU, and government contracts)
Owner: Legal Counsel
Participants: Requesting Department Head, Procurement (vendor contracts), Real Estate (leases), Finance (financial terms), VP Legal (high-value contracts), External Counsel
Source: workflow W688 — Contract &amp; Agreement Lifecycle Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W688_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W688_Lane1" name="Department Head">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W688_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W688_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W688_Lane2" name="Legal Assistant">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W688_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W688_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W688_Lane3" name="Legal Counsel">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W688_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W688_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W688_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W688_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W688_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W688_Lane4" name="Contract Owner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W688_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W688_Lane5" name="VP Legal">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W688_Task17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W688_End18</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W688_Start7" name="New contract or agreement required; existing contract approaching renewal/expiry…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W688_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W688_Task8" name="Contract request intake">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Contract request intake: Department Head submits contract request via legal portal: contract type (vendor, lease, service, customer, government, partnership), counterparty name, business purpose, estimated value, desired term, key commercial terms, target execution date
Responsible (R): Department Head
Accountable (A): Legal Counsel
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W688_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W688_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W688_Task9" name="Counterparty due diligence">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Counterparty due diligence: Legal or Compliance verifies counterparty: SEC/DTI registration check, BIR tax compliance (2303 certificate), litigation search, sanctions screening, existing relationship check (are there existing contracts with this counterparty across any BuildRight entity); for vendors: integrate with W620 vendor due diligence results
Responsible (R): Legal Assistant
Accountable (A): Legal Counsel
Duration: 2-4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W688_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W688_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W688_Task10" name="Contract drafting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Contract drafting: Legal Counsel drafts contract using approved template per W687; incorporates BuildRight standard terms and conditions, Philippine law governing clause, BIR-compliant invoicing requirements, data privacy provisions per RA 10173, and force majeure clause (typhoon, earthquake, pandemic); for standard-value contracts below threshold: use pre-approved template with minimal customization
Responsible (R): Legal Counsel
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 2-8 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W688_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W688_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W688_Task11" name="Internal review &amp; negotiation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Internal review &amp; negotiation: route contract to relevant stakeholders: Finance (payment terms, financial guarantees), Procurement (SLA metrics, delivery terms), IT (data privacy, technology clauses), Department Head (business terms); collect redlines and consolidate into negotiation position
Responsible (R): Legal Counsel
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 2-5 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W688_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W688_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W688_Task12" name="Counterparty negotiation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Counterparty negotiation: Legal Counsel or Department Head negotiates final terms with counterparty; all redlines tracked in the CLM (DOC-011); significant deviations from BuildRight standard terms flagged for VP Legal approval
Responsible (R): Legal Counsel / Department Head
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 1-14 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W688_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W688_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W688_Task13" name="Approval &amp; execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Approval &amp; execution: final contract routed for approval per DOA matrix per W686: contract value &lt;PHP 1M: Department Head + Legal Counsel; PHP 1M-10M: VP + CFO; &gt;PHP 10M: CEO + Board resolution per W243; executed via digital signature per W686 or wet-ink notarization if required by law (Philippine notarization required for real property leases &gt;1 year, government contracts above threshold)
Responsible (R): Legal Counsel
Accountable (A): VP Legal / CEO
Duration: 1-3 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W688_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W688_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W688_Task14" name="Contract registration &amp; obligation setup">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Contract registration &amp; obligation setup: executed contract registered in the CLM (DOC-011): key dates (commencement, expiry, renewal notice deadline), financial obligations (payment schedule, rate escalation), SLA metrics, special conditions; system sets up automated reminders for renewal notice deadlines (90, 60, 30 days before expiry)
Responsible (R): Legal Assistant
Accountable (A): Legal Counsel
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W688_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W688_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W688_Task15" name="Contract performance monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Contract performance monitoring: monthly, contract owner reviews SLA compliance and commercial performance against contracted terms; for vendor contracts: integrate with W669 vendor contract compliance; for lease agreements: integrate with W635 PFRS 16 lease accounting; for service contracts: review deliverable completion and SLA metrics
Responsible (R): Contract Owner / Department Head
Accountable (A): Legal Counsel
Duration: 2-4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W688_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W688_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W688_Task16" name="Renewal, amendment, or termination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Renewal, amendment, or termination: 90 days before expiry, system alerts contract owner and Legal: (a) renewal: if performance satisfactory, initiate renewal per original or revised terms; negotiate rate adjustments (escalation clauses, market rate review); (b) amendment: document changes via formal amendment or change order signed by both parties; (c) termination: if performance unsatisfactory or business need ended, Legal issues termination notice per contract terms; manage transition/exit obligations
Responsible (R): Legal Counsel / Contract Owner
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 2-5 days per renewal/termination</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W688_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W688_Flow30</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W688_Task17" name="Annual contract portfolio review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 10: Annual contract portfolio review: VP Legal and CFO conduct annual review of total contract portfolio: contract value by category, renewal pipeline, expiry concentration risk (too many contracts expiring simultaneously), standard term compliance rate, contract disputes summary, litigation exposure
Responsible (R): VP Legal / CFO
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 1 day/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W688_Flow30</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W688_Flow31</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W688_End18" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W688_Flow31</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W688_Annotation19">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-333 (ensure controlled execution — Document &amp; Knowledge Management (PA-30.3).) | - operational: Legal Counsel review and approval gate
Owner: Legal Counsel</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W688_Assoc20" sourceRef="W688_Annotation19" targetRef="W688_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
