    <bpmn:process id="W_W1483" name="W1483. Vendor Document Portal, Compliance Certificate Tracking &amp; Expiration Alert Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New vendor onboarding per W36; vendor compliance certificate approaching expiration; or regulatory audit requiring vendor documentation
Frequency: ~50–80 new vendor document sets/year; ~600 certificate renewals/year across ~800–1,000 vendors (~50/month per the staffing line)
Volume: ~1,000 active vendors each maintaining 3–8 compliance documents (business registration, tax compliance, product certifications, insurance, import permits) = ~3,000–8,000 tracked documents
Owner: Procurement Manager
Participants: Buyer, Vendor Account Manager, VP Legal, Compliance Officer, AP Accountant
Source: workflow W1483 — Vendor Document Portal, Compliance Certificate Tracking &amp; Expiration Alert Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1483_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1483_Lane1" name="Buyer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1483_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1483_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1483_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1483_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1483_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1483_Lane3" name="Vendor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1483_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1483_Lane4" name="Procurement Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1483_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1483_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1483_Start6" name="New vendor onboarding per W36; vendor compliance certificate approaching expiration; or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1483_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1483_Task7" name="Document collection during onboarding">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Document collection during onboarding: During vendor onboarding per W36: (a) Buyer provides vendor with access to BuildRight&#x27;s Vendor Document Portal (part of vendor portal per VS-03.4); (b) vendor uploads required compliance documents: (i) system validates: file format (PDF/image), file size, document type selection, (ii) system extracts key metadata via OCR: document type, issuing authority, issue date, expiration date; (c) Procurement Manager reviews uploaded documents: (i) verify document is current (not expired), (ii) verify document matches vendor legal name per SEC/DTI registration, (iii) approve or reject with reason (e.g., &quot; blurry document — please re-upload clear copy&quot;); (d) once all required documents approved: vendor status set to &quot;Compliant&quot; — eligible for PO issuance per W2
Responsible (R): Buyer / Vendor / Procurement Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 30 min/vendor</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1483_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1483_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1483_Task8" name="Expiration monitoring &amp; alerts">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Expiration monitoring &amp; alerts: (a) system continuously monitors document expiration dates: (i) 90 days before expiration: automated email to vendor via portal — &quot;Your [document type] expires on [date]. Please upload renewal.&quot;; (ii) 30 days before expiration: escalation email to Buyer — &quot;Vendor [name] has [document type] expiring in 30 days. Follow up with vendor.&quot;; (iii) at expiration: system flags vendor as &quot;Compliance Expired&quot; — warning displayed on all open POs; (iv) 30 days after expiration: system blocks new PO creation for the vendor until document is renewed; (b) Buyer follows up with vendor on expired documents via phone/email and logs communication in the portal
Responsible (R): System / Buyer
Accountable (A): Procurement Manager
Duration: Automated + 15 min/follow-up</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1483_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1483_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1483_Task9" name="Vendor document renewal processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Vendor document renewal processing: (a) vendor uploads renewed document via portal; (b) Procurement Manager reviews renewed document: (i) verify new expiration date is in the future, (ii) verify document details match vendor master data (name, TIN, address), (iii) approve renewal; (c) system updates vendor compliance status: &quot;Compliance Expired&quot; → &quot;Compliant&quot; (removes PO block if applicable); (d) system archives expired document with retention per W256 (10 years for tax documents, 3 years for insurance certificates)
Responsible (R): Vendor / Procurement Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 15 min/renewal</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1483_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1483_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1483_Task10" name="Compliance reporting for audits">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Compliance reporting for audits: (a) quarterly: Procurement Manager generates vendor compliance report: (i) total vendors by compliance status (Compliant, Expiring Soon, Expired, Blocked), (ii) vendors with multiple expired documents (high-risk), (iii) compliance rate by document type (which certificate type has the lowest renewal rate?); (b) VP Legal reviews vendor compliance report for regulatory risk; (c) for BIR audit preparation per W22.2: Procurement Manager produces vendor tax compliance documentation package: vendor TIN, BIR registration certificate, tax clearance for top 50 vendors (representing ~80% of spend)
Responsible (R): Procurement Manager / VP Legal
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1483_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1483_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1483_Task11" name="Product certification tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Product certification tracking: (a) for products requiring PS Mark, FDA notification, or other product-level certifications: system links product certification to both vendor and SKU; (b) if product certification expires: (i) system flags affected SKUs, (ii) POS can continue selling existing inventory (product was certified when manufactured), (iii) new POs for affected SKUs blocked until vendor provides updated certification, (iv) if certification is revoked (safety issue): trigger W1347 recall assessment
Responsible (R): System / Buyer
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1483_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1483_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1483_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1483_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1483_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-333 (ensure controlled execution — Document &amp; Knowledge Management (PA-30.3).) | - operational: requiring Procurement Manager approval for block overrides; operational: must handle multiple document calendars per vendor
Owner: Procurement Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1483_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1483_Annotation13" targetRef="W1483_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
