      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1484_Start5" name="New employee onboarding per W19.1; employee role change; or annual competency…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1484_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1484_Task6" name="Role-based curriculum design">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Role-based curriculum design: HR Training Manager maintains 8 role-based training curricula: (a) Cashier: POS operation (W5B), cash handling (W541), customer service basics, return processing (W12), age-restricted product prompts, multi-tender transactions, loss prevention awareness (W842); (b) Sales Associate: product knowledge by department, customer assistance, loyalty enrollment (W17), BOPIS pickup (W708), social selling basics (W1469); (c) Stock Associate: receiving procedures (W3), replenishment, cycle counting (W42), hazmat awareness per W142, forklift safety (DC), rental tool operations (W139); (d) Department Supervisor: team leadership, merchandising standards (W86), planogram compliance, project estimation basics (W1090), safety briefings (W1319), daily management (W5A); (e) CSR: customer service excellence, return processing (W12), complaint handling (W13), BOPIS fulfillment (W708), trade account basics; (f) Maintenance/Utility: store maintenance (W47), safety systems, basic repair, cleaning standards, hazmat spill response (W142); (g) DC Warehouse Associate: WMS operation, pick/pack/ship, RF scanner operation, safety, forklift certification; (h) HQ roles: department-specific modules (finance, merchandising, IT, HR, marketing, supply chain)
Responsible (R): HR Training Manager
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: Quarterly review (4 hours/quarter)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1484_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1484_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1484_Task7" name="New hire training path activation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: New hire training path activation: During onboarding per W19.1: (a) HR system triggers OLA enrollment in the appropriate role-based curriculum; (b) new employee&#x27;s OLA dashboard shows: (i) required courses (mandatory for role), (ii) recommended courses (elective enrichment), (iii) due dates (Day 1–5: company orientation and safety, Day 6–15: role-specific technical training, Day 16–30: advanced topics and on-floor practice); (c) system tracks completion and scores per course
Responsible (R): System / HR Training Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager (store roles) / Department Head (HQ roles)
Duration: Automated setup</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1484_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1484_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1484_Task8" name="Training delivery &amp; on-floor practice">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Training delivery &amp; on-floor practice: (a) Digital courses (OLA): policy modules, product knowledge videos, system simulations (POS practice mode), safety training with quiz; (b) In-person training (by Department Supervisor): hands-on POS practice, receiving dock walkthrough, product location tour, customer service role-play; (c) Buddy shifts (first 5 working days): new employee paired with experienced colleague for real-time coaching — buddy logs daily progress in OLA; (d) Department Supervisor check-ins: Day 7, Day 14, Day 30 — supervisor assesses progress, provides feedback, adjusts training pace
Responsible (R): New Employee / Department Supervisor / Buddy
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: First 30 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1484_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1484_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1484_Task9" name="Competency assessment &amp; certification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Competency assessment &amp; certification: (a) at Day 30: new employee completes role-based competency assessment in OLA: (i) knowledge quiz (minimum 80% pass required), (ii) practical skills checklist verified by Department Supervisor (POS operation, receiving procedure, customer interaction), (iii) safety certification quiz (100% pass required for safety-critical items); (b) if employee passes: &quot;Certified&quot; status — authorized for independent work without supervision; (c) if employee fails knowledge quiz: retake allowed within 7 days after remedial study; if fails again: HR Training Manager intervenes with coaching plan; (d) if employee fails practical skills: extended buddy period (additional 2 weeks) with targeted skill development
Responsible (R): New Employee / Department Supervisor / HR Training Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours/employee</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1484_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1484_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1484_Task10" name="Annual competency reassessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Annual competency reassessment: (a) all employees complete annual competency reassessment per W51: (i) updated policy and procedure refresher, (ii) safety recertification (mandatory for all), (iii) product knowledge update (new products, seasonal changes), (iv) system update training (if ERP/POS updated during year); (b) employees not meeting minimum competency: targeted remedial training within 30 days; (c) assessment results factor into annual performance review per W19.3
Responsible (R): HR Training Manager / System
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: ~2 hours/employee/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1484_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1484_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1484_Task11" name="Curriculum continuous improvement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Curriculum continuous improvement: (a) quarterly: HR Training Manager reviews training effectiveness: (i) competency pass rates by role and location, (ii) time-to-certification (days from hire to &quot;Certified&quot;), (iii) new hire turnover within first 90 days (indicator of onboarding quality), (iv) supervisor feedback on new hire readiness; (b) update curriculum based on: (i) new system features (ERP/POS updates require new training modules), (ii) incident learnings (safety incidents per W140 generate new safety training content), (iii) product changes (new product categories require updated product knowledge modules)
Responsible (R): HR Training Manager
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 4 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1484_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1484_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1484_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1484_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1484_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-333 (ensure controlled execution — Document &amp; Knowledge Management (PA-30.3).) | - operational: mobile-friendly OLA delivery and in-person alternatives for critical modules; operational: updates occur 2–3 times/year, requiring training content updates to match; operational: practical skills assessment as the primary certification gate
Owner: HR Training Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
